**What changed:**

| # | Problem | Fix |
|---|---------|-----|
| 1 | `npsp__DataImportProcessor.process(importIds)` — treated the batchable class as a static utility; compiler couldn't resolve it that way and reported "Variable does not exist." | Instantiated the batch class with the set of import IDs and submitted it via `Database.executeBatch(processor, 200)`. In a test context the caller wraps the call with `Test.startBatch()` / `Test.stopBatch()` so the batch completes before the results query runs, keeping everything in one transaction. |
| 2 | `String.equals(a, b)` — Apex `String` has no static two-arg `equals`. | Replaced with `processed.npsp__Status__c == 'Imported'`, which is the idiomatic Apex comparison (and is null-safe: `null == 'Imported'` is `false`). |

